---
import SiteLayout from '../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';

const base = `${import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '')}/`;
---

<SiteLayout title="Source provenance | ArcadeDuck" description="ArcadeDuck's recorded source lineage, file-level exceptions, and pre-release provenance audit.">
  <section class="page-hero about-hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Source History</p>
    <h1>Source provenance</h1>
    <p class="page-description">The recorded lineage and cleanup behind the initial public source release.</p>
    <p><a href={`${base}about/`}>Back to the ArcadeDuck story &rarr;</a></p>
  </section>
  <article class="about-page">
    <section class="about-section">
      <p class="eyebrow">Audited source provenance</p>
      <h2>Where the current ArcadeDuck source actually comes from.</h2>

      <p>
        ArcadeDuck is built on DuckStation source. The current lineage is not
        inferred from dates, similar files, or old project descriptions. It was
        reconstructed directly from the repository's Git graph during an
        extensive provenance audit.
      </p>

      <div class="lineage" aria-label="ArcadeDuck active source lineage">
        <a
          class="lineage-step"
          href="https://github.com/stenzek/duckstation/commit/2149ab4d6955bfa60cd56856aeb05aebef9e4a1a"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noreferrer"
        >
          <span class="lineage-label">Inherited root</span>
          <strong>DuckStation</strong>
          <span><code>2149ab4d6955bfa60cd56856aeb05aebef9e4a1a</code></span>
        </a>

        <span class="lineage-arrow" aria-hidden="true">&darr;</span>

        <a
          class="lineage-step"
          href="https://github.com/stenzek/duckstation/commit/25bc8a64803df7e702db66e0f11d7b7d0fdc99f2"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noreferrer"
        >
          <span class="lineage-label">Last inherited DuckStation commit</span>
          <strong>GPL-era Git boundary</strong>
          <span><code>25bc8a64803df7e702db66e0f11d7b7d0fdc99f2</code></span>
        </a>

        <span class="lineage-arrow" aria-hidden="true">&darr;</span>

        <div class="lineage-step lineage-current">
          <span class="lineage-label">First ArcadeDuck commit</span>
          <strong>ArcadeDuck active lineage</strong>
          <span><code>53f4ae558af0d569143d7ef7698f1328b71cdec7</code></span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p>
        The first ArcadeDuck commit,
        <code>53f4ae558af0d569143d7ef7698f1328b71cdec7</code>,
        has exactly one parent:
        <code>25bc8a64803df7e702db66e0f11d7b7d0fdc99f2</code>.
        That establishes the active project's inherited DuckStation boundary
        directly from repository history.
      </p>

      <p>
        The following historical DuckStation commit,
        <code>9ca6b5430fb358b39f21ce0b2fc0268de954dd23</code>,
        changed the project's source licensing. The audit therefore treats
        <code>25bc8a6</code> as the Git-graph boundary &mdash; not as a blanket
        claim that every individual file at that revision carried the same
        license.
      </p>

      <div class="about-links">
        <a
          href="https://github.com/stenzek/duckstation/commit/25bc8a64803df7e702db66e0f11d7b7d0fdc99f2"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noreferrer"
        >Inherited DuckStation boundary &#8599;</a>

        <a
          href="https://github.com/stenzek/duckstation/commit/9ca6b5430fb358b39f21ce0b2fc0268de954dd23"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noreferrer"
        >Following licensing-change commit &#8599;</a>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="about-section">
      <p class="eyebrow">The five-file exception</p>
      <h2>The boundary had five file-level exceptions.</h2>

      <p>
        The repository-level license at the inherited boundary was GPLv3, but
        the audit identified <strong>five source files</strong> that already
        carried <code>PolyForm-Strict-1.0.0</code>-only SPDX headers before the
        broader project licensing change.
      </p>

      <div class="about-code-card">
        <span>PolyForm-only audio rewrite</span>
        <code>00634f68cc0fc187068c9df08a4ea3564938c60a</code>
        <strong>
          src/util/audio_stream.cpp<br />
          src/util/audio_stream.h
        </strong>
      </div>

      <div class="about-code-card">
        <span>PolyForm-only software rasterizer split</span>
        <code>25bc8a64803df7e702db66e0f11d7b7d0fdc99f2</code>
        <strong>
          src/core/gpu_sw_rasterizer.cpp<br />
          src/core/gpu_sw_rasterizer.h<br />
          src/core/gpu_sw_rasterizer.inl
        </strong>
      </div>

      <p>
        That is why ArcadeDuck does not describe <code>25bc8a6</code> as simply
        "the last GPL version." It is the correct Git boundary, but those five
        file-level exceptions required separate treatment.
      </p>

      <p class="about-punchline">
        Apparently even the clean boundary had a boundary condition.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section class="about-section">
      <p class="eyebrow">Historical cleanup</p>
      <h2>The five exceptions were removed or restored before the first public release.</h2>

      <div class="about-code-card">
        <span>Restoration / removal commit</span>
        <code>3f119ddfc13d51ad68d5134ef09fde54ae23315b</code>
        <strong>August 27, 2026</strong>
      </div>

      <p>
        That commit removed the separate PolyForm-era software rasterizer and
        restored the older software-rendering path. The two audio files were
        substantially restored to the earlier implementation that carried a GPL
        licensing alternative, then continued forward with ArcadeDuck's own
        audio changes.
      </p>

      <p>
        The provenance audit compared the restored source against both the older
        implementation and the intervening PolyForm rewrite. Its normalized
        comparison found{' '}
        <strong>zero retained lines
        unique to the PolyForm rewrite</strong> in the compared current
        audio/backend implementations, while hundreds of meaningful lines
        matched the older implementation.
      </p>

      <p>
        The audited source contained no
        <code>PolyForm-Strict-1.0.0</code>-only or
        <code>CC-BY-NC-ND-4.0</code>-only SPDX declarations in the scanned
        current text headers.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section class="about-section">
      <p class="eyebrow">Earlier proof of concept</p>
      <h2>Arcade1Up and t-dollaz are part of the history, not the current Git ancestry.</h2>

      <p>
        ArcadeDuck's earliest proof-of-concept work used the{' '}
        <strong>Arcade1Up Simpsons Bowling DuckStation fork</strong> and the
        later <strong>t-dollaz desktop continuation</strong>. Those projects
        were important references for understanding the cabinet-specific
        hardware and getting the original Simpsons Bowling experiment moving.
      </p>

      <p>
        The provenance audit confirmed that the older proof-of-concept is a{' '}
        <strong>separate snapshot history</strong>. It is not an ancestor of
        the current ArcadeDuck <code>dev</code> lineage.
      </p>

      <p>
        They remain credited because they are genuinely part of ArcadeDuck's
        history. They are simply no longer presented as the Git ancestry of the
        source tree being released today.
      </p>

      <div class="about-links">
        <a
          href="https://github.com/Arcade1Up/duckstation-sb"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noreferrer"
        >Arcade1Up / duckstation-sb &#8599;</a>

        <a
          href="https://github.com/t-dollaz/simpsons-bowling-baby-phoenix-duckstation"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noreferrer"
        >t-dollaz continuation &#8599;</a>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="about-section">
      <p class="eyebrow">Repository-wide review</p>
      <h2>Provenance was checked, not assumed.</h2>

      <p>
        The provenance review enumerated all{' '}
        <strong>2,145 tracked files</strong> in the audited checkout and
        scanned tracked text for SPDX identifiers, copyright notices, license
        text, and upstream/reference markers.
      </p>

      <p>
        Reachable history, branch tips, historical license changes, candidate
        upstream matches, third-party notices, source attribution, and the
        identified file-level licensing exceptions were then reviewed in
        detail.
      </p>

      <p>
        Even minor or possible findings were remediated before the public
        repository was created. The public repository was then started from the
        verified clean source snapshot instead of publishing the old forensic
        development history.
      </p>

      <div class="about-code-card">
        <span>Initial clean public source commit</span>
        <code>13a1d6a02428efe4ec00e531ccd8e29c1fd0bc0e</code>
        <strong>Initial public source release</strong>
      </div>

      <p class="about-punchline">
        Trust is useful. Reproducible commit hashes are considerably more useful.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</SiteLayout>
